  "question": {
    "text": "<p>When a certain biased die is rolled, a particular face occurs with probability <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></math> and its opposite face occurs with probability <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;All other faces occur with probability <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mo>.</mo></math></p><p>Note that opposite faces sum to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn></math> in any die. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;and the probability of obtaining total sum <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo></math> when such a die is rolled twice, is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>13</mn><mn>96</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;then the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is</p>"
